CREATE TABLE users (
    id INT AUTO_INCREMENT PRIMARY KEY,
    name VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    email VARCHAR(100) UNIQUE NOT NULL,
    gender ENUM('Male', 'Female', 'Other'),
    date_of_birth DATE,
    created_at TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
);

==============================================================================

==> AUTO_INCREMENT
Automatically generates the next number whenever a new row is inserted.

==> PRIMARY KEY
Identifies each row uniquely.

==> VARCHAR(100)
VARCHAR means variable-length character/string.

==> NOT NULL
Means this column must have a value.

==> UNIQUE
Means duplicate values aren't allowed.

==> ENUM
It means the column can only contain values from a predefined list.

==> TIMESTAMP
A data type used to store a date and time.

==> DEFAULT
Defines a value that MySQL should automatically use if you don't provide one.

